# Inbox and leads (signed in; see auth.http). Items appear when a widget visitor asks
# something the bot couldn't answer (widget.http); leads when a visitor leaves an email.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api
@origin = http://localhost:3000
@botId = PASTE_BOT_ID_HERE
@itemId = PASTE_ITEM_ID_HERE

### Open questions (?status=done for answered ones); Free shows the last 7 days
GET {{baseUrl}}/bots/{{botId}}/inbox

### One question with the conversation it came from
GET {{baseUrl}}/bots/{{botId}}/inbox/{{itemId}}

### Teach your bot — the answer becomes a knowledge source, the item is done
POST {{baseUrl}}/bots/{{botId}}/inbox/{{itemId}}/answer
Origin: {{origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "answer": "Yes, we sell green and black tea."
}

### Dismiss (done) or reopen (open)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/bots/{{botId}}/inbox/{{itemId}}
Origin: {{origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "done"
}

### Visitors who left an email
GET {{baseUrl}}/bots/{{botId}}/leads

### CSV export — Business only, otherwise 402 upgrade_required
GET {{baseUrl}}/bots/{{botId}}/leads.csv

### Overview numbers: totals, previous period, daily chart, top questions, "Needs you"
# days=1..90 (default 7); tz is any IANA name, unknown values fall back to UTC.
GET {{baseUrl}}/bots/{{botId}}/stats?days=7&tz=Europe/Berlin
